  "query_mode": "unanchored",
  "ranked": [
    {
      "body": "Every state transition on a payment must produce an audit event in the \`payment_audit_events\` table. The \`AuditLogger.record\` method is the only path; do not write to the table directly. See \`src/payments/audit.ts\`.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/audit.md > Section: Payment audit logging > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "557acc192dbf5d2b",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "audit",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 2.1756,
      "tokens": 49,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "If a refund is submitted twice, the second call should not create a new ledger
row. Instead, correlate the repeated call with the original payment audit event
and reuse the existing reconciliation record.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/reconciliation.md > Section: Refund reconciliation > Duplicate refund handling > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "e8541738dd521814",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/reconciliation.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "reconciliation",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "ReconciliationService.reconcileRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.2575,
      "tokens": 39,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "We use the upstream provider's idempotency key as the source of truth for retry semantics. This avoids a per-service deduplication store and aligns with how providers retry on transient failures.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/adr/0001-idempotency-keys.md > Section: ADR-0001: Idempotency keys for payment retries > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "01121fc4726eb675",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "decision",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.1528,
      "tokens": 40,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Every refund attempt must emit an audit event, including failed attempts. The \`RefundService.processRefund\` method is the only entry point and must be idempotent — providers may retry it, and a duplicate call for the same order should return the existing refund record rather than creating a new one.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/refunds.md > Section: Refunds > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "4010ec0e9bdd96d7",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/refund.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "refunds",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "RefundService.processRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.1495,
      "tokens": 61,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Subscriptions follow a lifecycle: \`active → canceling → canceled\` for cancellations, and \`active → upgrading → active\` for plan upgrades. Every state transition is logged to the \`billing_audit_events\` table.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/billing/subscriptions.md > Section: Subscriptions > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "ee127d7db1fc0ece",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/billing/subscription.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "subscriptions",
        "project": "billing",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "SubscriptionService.cancel",
          "SubscriptionService.upgrade",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.345,
      "tokens": 44,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Every support escalation must write an audit event before notification so operators can reconstruct who escalated the incident and why.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/support/escalations.md > Section: Support escalations > Audit > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "21e070d4b1adbce8",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/support/escalations.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "escalations",
        "project": "support",
        "routes": [
          "POST /support/escalations",
        ],
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "EscalationService.open",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.2974,
      "tokens": 21,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "1. Identify the affected domain: payments, billing, auth, notifications, or platform-wide.
2. Pull recent audit events from the relevant audit table (\`payment_audit_events\`, \`billing_audit_events\`).
3. Check for elevated retry rates on idempotent operations like refunds, invoice creation, or webhook dispatch.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/incident-runbook.md > Section: Incident response runbook > Initial triage > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "b15775bba4a62e62",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.2966,
      "tokens": 63,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- **Audit event** — a record of a state change. Payment audit events live in payments; billing audit events live in billing.
- **Capture** — the act of finalizing a draft invoice and triggering payment collection. See billing for the canonical capture rules.
- **Dispatch** — outbound delivery of a webhook event to an external endpoint.
- **Idempotency key** — a stable token used to deduplicate retries of the same operation. Used by refunds, invoices, and notifications.
- **Permission** — an authorization atom held by a principal. Checked via PermissionChecker.can.
- **Reconciliation** — the process of correlating two records that should refer to the same underlying event.
- **Refund** — the reversal of a payment. Implemented by RefundService.processRefund.
- **Session** — an authenticated request context. Stored via SessionStore.get and renewed via POST /sessions/:id/renew.
- **Subscription** — a recurring billing relationship. Lifecycle: active, canceling, upgrading, canceled.
- **Token** — an API credential. Issued via TokenStore.issue and revoked via TokenStore.revoke.
- **Webhook** — an outbound HTTP callback to a customer endpoint.

This glossary is provided for orientation only. None of the rules above are authoritative — every term has a canonical doc in its own module.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/glossary.md > Section: Glossary > Domain terms > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "d161a116ca4719a5",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.2186,
      "tokens": 275,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "The deduplication window is 24 hours. An \`idempotency_key\` older than 24 hours is treated as a new send and reuses the same key only for logging correlation.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/notifications/email.md > Section: Email notifications > Deduplication window > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "ac1d370edd9a06b2",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/notifications/email.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "email",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "EmailWorker.send",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.1652,
      "tokens": 40,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Methods that mutate state should be named with verbs. Methods that read state should use noun-style names where appropriate.

- \`processRefund\` — verb, mutating
- \`reconcileRefund\` — verb, mutating
- \`record\` — verb (used by \`AuditLogger.record\`)
- \`can\` — predicate (used by \`PermissionChecker.can\`)
- \`get\` — accessor (used by \`SessionStore.get\`)",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/style-guide.md > Section: Code style guide > Method naming > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "70cd3ec356967ca4",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.0535,
      "tokens": 88,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Endpoints must tolerate duplicate deliveries. Each payload includes an \`event_id\` field that is stable across retries — receivers should use \`event_id\` as the deduplication key.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/notifications/webhooks.md > Section: Webhooks > Deduplication > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "d8eef556768aaee1",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/notifications/webhook.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "webhooks",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "WebhookDispatcher.dispatch",
          "WebhookDispatcher.retry",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.1129,
      "tokens": 35,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "\`InvoiceService.capture\` finalizes a draft invoice and triggers payment collection. Once captured, an invoice is **immutable** — line items must not be modified after capture. Only status transitions are permitted on a captured invoice.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/billing/invoices.md > Section: Invoices > Capture > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "d9e8deaa2c217935",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/billing/invoice.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "invoices",
        "project": "billing",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "InvoiceService.create",
          "InvoiceService.capture",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.0887,
      "tokens": 44,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "We chose **at-least-once** delivery over exactly-once because exactly-once requires a distributed coordinator that adds operational complexity and latency. Customers must implement idempotent handlers on their side using the \`event_id\` field.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/adr/0002-webhook-idempotency.md > Section: ADR-0002: Webhook delivery uses at-least-once semantics > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "9f9ffdd07be1e2b9",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "decision",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.0689,
      "tokens": 47,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- \`AuditLogger.record\` now writes the \`actor\` field unconditionally.
- \`WebhookDispatcher.dispatch\` retry schedule shortened on first attempt.
- \`TokenStore.revoke\` returns the previous revocation timestamp on idempotent calls.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/release-notes.md > Section: Release notes > v1.3.2 > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "6fe661858d72c616",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.0666,
      "tokens": 49,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Each event captures actor, action, before-state, after-state, and a reason string. Missing fields fail the schema check at write time.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/audit.md > Section: Payment audit logging > Required fields > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "ac0c0107c99f87c0",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "audit",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 1.6425,
      "tokens": 28,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Duplicate refunds must be reconciled against the original ledger entry. The
\`ReconciliationService.reconcileRefund\` method compares charge IDs, refund IDs,
and audit trail entries before posting a corrective ledger line.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/reconciliation.md > Section: Refund reconciliation > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "9e239bfb8a5b9199",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/reconciliation.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "reconciliation",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "ReconciliationService.reconcileRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.0826,
      "tokens": 43,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "\`RefundService.processRefund\` and the charge path both rely on the provider key being present in the request. Callers without an idempotency key must generate one before invoking either path.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/adr/0001-idempotency-keys.md > Section: ADR-0001: Idempotency keys for payment retries > Consequences > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "e613695059a98a4e",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "decision",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.1159,
      "tokens": 41,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "A partial refund reuses the same idempotency key. See \`src/payments/refund.ts\` for the canonical implementation. Partial refunds must be ledgered against the original charge.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/refunds.md > Section: Refunds > Partial refunds > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "d3357aa37fc4b9a0",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/refund.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "refunds",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "RefundService.processRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.1023,
      "tokens": 38,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "When a payment is partially refunded twice, the second call should return the existing refund record. Set \`STRIPE_API_KEY\` before running \`refund.test.ts\` to verify this end-to-end.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/refunds.md > Section: Refunds > Edge cases > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "0abdabd1da6b101e",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/refund.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "refunds",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "RefundService.processRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.0954,
      "tokens": 40,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "All subscription state transitions — including cancellation and upgrade — are recorded in \`billing_audit_events\`. The \`before_state\`, \`after_state\`, and \`actor\` fields are required. Writes go through the subscription service only; do not write to \`billing_audit_events\` directly.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/billing/subscriptions.md > Section: Subscriptions > Billing audit > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "e8aabe8df9e36300",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/billing/subscription.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "subscriptions",
        "project": "billing",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "SubscriptionService.cancel",
          "SubscriptionService.upgrade",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.2895,
      "tokens": 54,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- Look for failed \`RefundService.processRefund\` retries in the last hour.
- Check \`ReconciliationService.reconcileRefund\` for duplicate ledger rows.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/incident-runbook.md > Section: Incident response runbook > Common checks by domain > Payments > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "03725251557895d6",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.176,
      "tokens": 35,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- Look for \`InvoiceService.create\` errors on the \`billing_period\` field.
- Check subscription state transitions in \`billing_audit_events\`.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/incident-runbook.md > Section: Incident response runbook > Common checks by domain > Billing > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "5a5ce6bf06b9d8af",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.1457,
      "tokens": 28,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Service classes use the \`XxxService\` suffix. Repository classes use \`XxxStore\`. Workers use \`XxxWorker\`. Examples:

- \`RefundService\` — payments domain
- \`InvoiceService\` — billing domain
- \`SubscriptionService\` — billing domain
- \`SessionStore\` — auth domain
- \`TokenStore\` — auth domain
- \`EmailWorker\` — notifications domain
- \`WebhookDispatcher\` — notifications domain (note: \`Dispatcher\` because it dispatches and retries)",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/style-guide.md > Section: Code style guide > Class naming > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "85855d74239f671b",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.0515,
      "tokens": 105,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Line items are written to the draft invoice before capture. All mutations to line items must happen before \`InvoiceService.capture\` is called. After capture, the \`invoice_line_items\` table is append-only for audit purposes.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/billing/invoices.md > Section: Invoices > Line items > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "8ab9e7d26702eae3",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/billing/invoice.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "invoices",
        "project": "billing",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "InvoiceService.create",
          "InvoiceService.capture",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.0711,
      "tokens": 44,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "If \`InvoiceService.create\` is called twice with the same \`billing_period\` for the same customer, the second call returns the existing draft invoice record and does not emit a second creation event.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/billing/invoices.md > Section: Invoices > Edge cases > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "08c69dae010adb68",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/billing/invoice.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
