      },
      "score": 0.7492,
      "tokens": 43,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "\`RefundService.processRefund\` and the charge path both rely on the provider key being present in the request. Callers without an idempotency key must generate one before invoking either path.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/adr/0001-idempotency-keys.md > Section: ADR-0001: Idempotency keys for payment retries > Consequences > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "e613695059a98a4e",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "decision",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.8381,
      "tokens": 41,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Webhook delivery uses an **at-least-once** guarantee. \`WebhookDispatcher.dispatch\` signs the payload with the endpoint's secret, writes the delivery attempt record to \`webhook_delivery_attempts\` before making the HTTP call, and returns the attempt ID. Writing first guarantees retries happen even if the process crashes after sending.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/notifications/webhooks.md > Section: Webhooks > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "73cc02f765510f3a",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/notifications/webhook.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "webhooks",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "WebhookDispatcher.dispatch",
          "WebhookDispatcher.retry",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.7991,
      "tokens": 66,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- **Audit event** — a record of a state change. Payment audit events live in payments; billing audit events live in billing.
- **Capture** — the act of finalizing a draft invoice and triggering payment collection. See billing for the canonical capture rules.
- **Dispatch** — outbound delivery of a webhook event to an external endpoint.
- **Idempotency key** — a stable token used to deduplicate retries of the same operation. Used by refunds, invoices, and notifications.
- **Permission** — an authorization atom held by a principal. Checked via PermissionChecker.can.
- **Reconciliation** — the process of correlating two records that should refer to the same underlying event.
- **Refund** — the reversal of a payment. Implemented by RefundService.processRefund.
- **Session** — an authenticated request context. Stored via SessionStore.get and renewed via POST /sessions/:id/renew.
- **Subscription** — a recurring billing relationship. Lifecycle: active, canceling, upgrading, canceled.
- **Token** — an API credential. Issued via TokenStore.issue and revoked via TokenStore.revoke.
- **Webhook** — an outbound HTTP callback to a customer endpoint.

This glossary is provided for orientation only. None of the rules above are authoritative — every term has a canonical doc in its own module.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/glossary.md > Section: Glossary > Domain terms > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "d161a116ca4719a5",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.508,
      "tokens": 275,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "1. Identify the affected domain: payments, billing, auth, notifications, or platform-wide.
2. Pull recent audit events from the relevant audit table (\`payment_audit_events\`, \`billing_audit_events\`).
3. Check for elevated retry rates on idempotent operations like refunds, invoice creation, or webhook dispatch.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/incident-runbook.md > Section: Incident response runbook > Initial triage > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "b15775bba4a62e62",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.4601,
      "tokens": 63,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Methods that mutate state should be named with verbs. Methods that read state should use noun-style names where appropriate.

- \`processRefund\` — verb, mutating
- \`reconcileRefund\` — verb, mutating
- \`record\` — verb (used by \`AuditLogger.record\`)
- \`can\` — predicate (used by \`PermissionChecker.can\`)
- \`get\` — accessor (used by \`SessionStore.get\`)",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/style-guide.md > Section: Code style guide > Method naming > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "70cd3ec356967ca4",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.3377,
      "tokens": 88,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "\`InvoiceService.create\` is idempotent. Using the same \`customer_id\` and \`billing_period\` as a natural key, a second call for the same period returns the existing draft invoice instead of creating a duplicate. Callers must pass a stable \`billing_period\` value.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/billing/invoices.md > Section: Invoices > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "e3265d14f576582e",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/billing/invoice.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "invoices",
        "project": "billing",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "InvoiceService.create",
          "InvoiceService.capture",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.2867,
      "tokens": 57,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "The deduplication window is 24 hours. An \`idempotency_key\` older than 24 hours is treated as a new send and reuses the same key only for logging correlation.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/notifications/email.md > Section: Email notifications > Deduplication window > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "ac1d370edd9a06b2",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/notifications/email.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "email",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "EmailWorker.send",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.3321,
      "tokens": 40,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "We chose **at-least-once** delivery over exactly-once because exactly-once requires a distributed coordinator that adds operational complexity and latency. Customers must implement idempotent handlers on their side using the \`event_id\` field.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/adr/0002-webhook-idempotency.md > Section: ADR-0002: Webhook delivery uses at-least-once semantics > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "9f9ffdd07be1e2b9",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "decision",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.2559,
      "tokens": 47,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Token rotation issues a new token via \`TokenStore.issue\` and revokes the old one via \`TokenStore.revoke\` in a single transaction. **Rotation is not idempotent** — calling it twice produces two new tokens and revokes two old ones. Callers must not retry rotation without user confirmation.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/auth/tokens.md > Section: API tokens > Rotation > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "dd8f143255d86cf3",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/auth/tokens.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "tokens",
        "project": "auth",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "TokenStore.issue",
          "TokenStore.revoke",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.2724,
      "tokens": 63,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- Added \`RefundService.processRefund\` retry guard on duplicate provider callbacks.
- Updated \`InvoiceService.create\` to accept a \`billing_period\` parameter.
- New route \`POST /sessions/:id/renew\` for session renewal.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/release-notes.md > Section: Release notes > v1.4.0 > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "9482060f72351df7",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.3758,
      "tokens": 49,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Every refund attempt must emit an audit event, including failed attempts. The \`RefundService.processRefund\` method is the only entry point and must be idempotent — providers may retry it, and a duplicate call for the same order should return the existing refund record rather than creating a new one.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/refunds.md > Section: Refunds > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "4010ec0e9bdd96d7",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/refund.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "refunds",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "RefundService.processRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 1.1901,
      "tokens": 61,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "When a payment is partially refunded twice, the second call should return the existing refund record. Set \`STRIPE_API_KEY\` before running \`refund.test.ts\` to verify this end-to-end.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/refunds.md > Section: Refunds > Edge cases > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "0abdabd1da6b101e",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/refund.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "refunds",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "RefundService.processRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.7503,
      "tokens": 40,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "If a refund is submitted twice, the second call should not create a new ledger
row. Instead, correlate the repeated call with the original payment audit event
and reuse the existing reconciliation record.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/payments/reconciliation.md > Section: Refund reconciliation > Duplicate refund handling > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "e8541738dd521814",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/payments/reconciliation.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "reconciliation",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "ReconciliationService.reconcileRefund",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.6966,
      "tokens": 39,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "We use the upstream provider's idempotency key as the source of truth for retry semantics. This avoids a per-service deduplication store and aligns with how providers retry on transient failures.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/adr/0001-idempotency-keys.md > Section: ADR-0001: Idempotency keys for payment retries > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "01121fc4726eb675",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "decision",
        "project": "payments",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.5161,
      "tokens": 40,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- Look for failed \`RefundService.processRefund\` retries in the last hour.
- Check \`ReconciliationService.reconcileRefund\` for duplicate ledger rows.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/incident-runbook.md > Section: Incident response runbook > Common checks by domain > Payments > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "03725251557895d6",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.4413,
      "tokens": 35,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Service classes use the \`XxxService\` suffix. Repository classes use \`XxxStore\`. Workers use \`XxxWorker\`. Examples:

- \`RefundService\` — payments domain
- \`InvoiceService\` — billing domain
- \`SubscriptionService\` — billing domain
- \`SessionStore\` — auth domain
- \`TokenStore\` — auth domain
- \`EmailWorker\` — notifications domain
- \`WebhookDispatcher\` — notifications domain (note: \`Dispatcher\` because it dispatches and retries)",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/general/style-guide.md > Section: Code style guide > Class naming > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "85855d74239f671b",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "project",
        "project": "general",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
      },
      "score": 0.1966,
      "tokens": 105,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "\`EmailWorker.send\` enqueues a transactional email job. Delivery is asynchronous — the method returns a job ID, not a delivery receipt. All transactional emails are **deduplicated by \`idempotency_key\`**: passing the same key twice enqueues the job once and returns the same job ID on the second call.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/notifications/email.md > Section: Email notifications > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "be3c09d3ea8775e6",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/notifications/email.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "email",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "EmailWorker.send",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.278,
      "tokens": 67,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "Failed delivery attempts are retried with exponential backoff: 1 min, 5 min, 30 min, 2 hr, 8 hr. After five failures the job is moved to the dead-letter queue and an alert fires. The \`idempotency_key\` prevents duplicate sends during retries.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/notifications/email.md > Section: Email notifications > Retry behavior > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "e9368861c74bb025",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "files": [
          "src/notifications/email.ts",
        ],
        "layer": "module",
        "module": "email",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
        },
        "symbols": [
          "EmailWorker.send",
        ],
      },
      "score": 0.2898,
      "tokens": 62,
      "type_bias_applied": false,
    },
    {
      "body": "- Customers must implement idempotent webhook handlers using \`event_id\` as the deduplication key.
- The at-least-once contract is documented in the public API reference.
- \`WebhookDispatcher.dispatch\` must write to \`webhook_delivery_attempts\` before any HTTP call; this ordering must not be changed.",
      "contexttrail": "Source: docs/adr/0002-webhook-idempotency.md > Section: ADR-0002: Webhook delivery uses at-least-once semantics > Consequences > Part: 1/1",
      "id": "c3ea984d0379b6c4",
      "kind": "chunk",
      "scope": {
        "layer": "decision",
        "project": "notifications",
        "source": {
          "config_rule": "docs-project-default",
          "frontmatter": true,
